(940882, 'Head of Accounting', 'https://www.jobfind.gr/JobAd/View/GR/Theseis_Ergasias/3a24d2e6-affa-4195-919a-fbd2080d0395/', 'ΚΕΝΤΡΟ ΑΘΗΝΑΣ | ΑΘΗΝΑ - ΑΤΤΙΚΗ', '2026-05-05', '2026-05-05 17:05:14', 'ONIRO HOTELS GROUP', ' Περιγραφή  Company  Description Oniro  Hotels envisions creating a portfolio of boutique hotels across  Greece and  Europe that serve as unique cultural landmarks.  Each property reflects the unique cultural identity of its locale, offering guests an authentic and memorable experience. With a commitment to excellence,  Oniro  Hotels combines luxury accommodations with personalized service to deliver exceptional hospitality. Join a company dedicated to preserving heritage while setting new standards in the boutique hotel industry. Role  Description This is a full-time, on-site role for the  Head of  Accounting, based in the  Athens  Metropolitan  Area.  The  Head of  Accounting will be the financial compass of  Oniro — responsible for the full accounting cycle, statutory compliance, and reporting integrity across the group. Own the  Monthly  Closing Drive the full month-end close process with precision and speed —  P& L, balance sheet, accruals, reconciliations. A A D E  Tax  Compliance &  Reporting Prepare and submit all required tax filings —  V A T, income tax, withholding tax — in full compliance with  A A D E regulations and  Greek tax law. Financial  Reporting &  Analysis Produce accurate, insightful monthly management accounts and ad-hoc financial reports for senior leadership. Statutory &  Legal  Compliance Navigate  Greek accounting law ( Ε Γ Λ Σ), ensure full compliance with all legal obligations including  G F P requirements and annual statutory filings. Cash  Flow &  Treasury  Support Monitor and forecast cash positions; support the  C F O on liquidity management and banking relationships. Audit  Readiness Maintain audit-ready books at all times.  Be the point of contact for external auditors and tax advisors.  Απαραίτητα  Προσόντα  Qualifications A -  Class  License  Accountant Proven experience in a senior accounting role Deep knowledge of  A A D E tax reporting Thorough understanding of regulatory requirements and compliance standards  Monthly closing mastery E R P proficiency Bachelor\'s degree in  Accounting,  Finance, or a related field Experience in the hospitality industry is preferred  Παροχές  What\'s  In  It  For  You Fair &  Transparent  Compensation Your package will be determined based on your actual skills, experience, and track record — not a rigid salary band.  We believe in paying people what they\'re truly worth.  Come with your number and let\'s have an honest conversation. Strategic seat at the table Report directly to senior leadership and help shape financial strategy — not just execute it. Athens-based, full-time', 'Πλήρης απασχόληση'),
(940883, 'Βοηθός Σερβιτόρου', 'https://www.jobfind.gr/JobAd/View/GR/Theseis_Ergasias/5bf8e54b-fb60-4a48-bb5b-243e76516135/', 'ΚΕΝΤΡΟ ΘΕΣΣΑΛΟΝΙΚΗΣ | ΘΕΣΣΑΛΟΝΙΚΗ', '2026-05-05', '2026-05-05 17:05:14', 'ΚΑΤΑΣΤΗΜΑ ΕΣΤΙΑΣΗΣ', ' Περιγραφή  Επισιτιστικό κατάστημα στο κέντρο της  Θεσσαλονίκης αναζητά βοηθούς σερβιτόρου για πλήρη και μερική απασχόληση.  Θα εκτιμηθεί προϋπηρεσία στην ειδικότητα.', 'Πλήρης απασχόληση | Μερική απασχόληση'),
